## Development Guidelines

### Adding New Settings
1. **Identify Category**: Determine appropriate section component
2. **Update Types**: Add interfaces to `types.ts`
3. **Implement UI**: Add controls to relevant section component
4. **Update Logic**: Extend useSettings hook if needed
5. **Test Integration**: Verify with both dev and production builds

### Component Structure Pattern
```typescript
export default function SectionSettings({ settings }: SettingsSectionProps) {
  const [localState, setLocalState] = useState();

  const handleChange = async (value: any) => {
    // Update local state
    setLocalState(value);

    // Persist via Tauri command
    await invoke("update_setting", { key: "setting_name", value });

    // Update global settings
    settings.refetchSettings();
  };

  return (
    <div className="space-y-6">
      <h3 className="text-lg font-medium text-gray-900 mb-4">Section Name</h3>
      {/* Settings controls */}
    </div>
  );
}
```

